proof.text:
Take $N=P_{02}M$ and $t=c^c_M$ in step 3. By step 2, the ordinary composite transpose of $c^c_M s_M$ is $d_N\eta^c_{02,M}$. The ambient application of [lem-weil-pbc-conjugate-iso-unit-equation], with $L_1=L_{12}L_{01}$ and $L_2=L_{02}$, says that the ordinary composite transpose of $c_M$ is $d_{L_{02}M}\eta_{02,M}$. Put $R=R_{10}R_{21}$. Postcomposition of a morphism $a$ by $k_{02,M}$ changes its ordinary transpose $R(a)\eta_{\mathrm{comp},M}$ to $R(k_{02,M})R(a)\eta_{\mathrm{comp},M}$, simply by functoriality. Therefore the transpose of $k_{02,M}c_M$ is
$$R(k_{02,M})d_{L_{02}M}\eta_{02,M}
=d_N R_{20}(k_{02,M})\eta_{02,M}
=d_N\eta^c_{02,M}.$$
The first equality is naturality of $d$ at the ambient morphism $k_{02,M}$; the second is step 1. The ordinary composite Hom bijection is injective, so the two morphisms $L_{12}L_{01}M\to P_{02}M$ coincide. This proves $c^c_M k_{12,P_{01}M}L_{12}(k_{01,M})=k_{02,M}c_M$, and also proves the stated equivalent inverse-transpose description.

